From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] page-fault slots change state by CAS; a queue destroy wakes the waiters it strands and disarms its area for 327

Upstream: not yet submitted; written to be upstreamed (generic, no title names)
Licence: MIT, as ps3recomp (see its LICENSE); offered under the same terms
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0035)

What (fixes to 0033 and 0035, from their review, I-1, M-2 and M-4):
- I-1: a fault slot's "detached" and "recovered" flags become one state word
  (waiting, recovered, detached, orphaned, freeing) changed by
  compare-and-swap. A 57 that lands while a host thread detaches (the
  pager's normal order: map, then 57 at once) left the slot taken for ever;
  now the thread sees "recovered" and frees it. The claim loop prints a line
  every 5 s while every slot is taken.
- M-2: sys_event_queue_destroy calls the page-fault hook before it drops the
  queue's events. A thread whose event is still queued there takes the abort
  path (a host thread whose page is mapped goes on), and a detached slot is
  freed; an event the pager already received is left alone. The area is left
  disarmed, and 327 for it arms it again with the new queue. The retry lines
  print the queue id they used.
- M-4: the "still waiting" seconds come from a monotonic clock
  (GetTickCount64), not a count of nominal 20 us naps.
Behaviour reference: RPCS3 sys_mmapper.cpp and Thread.cpp (GPL-2.0, read
only, no code from them). What lv2 does to a fault whose queue is destroyed
is not known (D59).
Tests: tests/test_mmapper_page_fault.c (100 rounds of map-then-57 against a
detaching host thread, each slot freed; a destroy with a queued PPU fault
aborts; 327 re-arms the disarmed area, then EBUSY).

